1
00:00:22,280 --> 00:00:23,550
What the...

2
00:00:24,240 --> 00:00:25,790
Are you kidding me?

3
00:00:25,790 --> 00:00:28,170
Just bring me back to life already.

4
00:00:28,170 --> 00:00:30,210
<i>I'm pretty sure I was...</i>

5
00:00:30,930 --> 00:00:34,210
<i>on my way to go skiing with my coworkers.</i>

6
00:00:38,410 --> 00:00:41,850
<i>So did our bus get into an accident?</i>

7
00:00:41,850 --> 00:00:43,560
<i>But my memories are...</i>

8
00:00:44,410 --> 00:00:48,900
<i>Are all the people standing 
in this line... dead?</i>

9
00:00:49,410 --> 00:00:51,020
Chief Igarashi...

10
00:00:56,130 --> 00:00:58,840
I will now begin guiding 
you all in order.

11
00:00:58,840 --> 00:01:01,120
Please proceed forward calmly.

12
00:01:08,260 --> 00:01:10,290
<i>She's here, too?</i>

13
00:01:10,290 --> 00:01:12,170
Next, please.

14
00:01:14,300 --> 00:01:16,600
Mr. Arihito Atobe?

15
00:01:16,970 --> 00:01:18,140
Uh, yes?

16
00:01:18,750 --> 00:01:20,680
Please take this.

17
00:01:22,430 --> 00:01:23,960
Once you arrive,

18
00:01:23,960 --> 00:01:27,550
go to the guild first 
and choose your job.

19
00:01:27,830 --> 00:01:28,930
Guild?

20
00:01:30,380 --> 00:01:31,450
Well, then...

21
00:01:40,500 --> 00:01:43,240
Welcome to Labyrinth Country!

22
00:01:44,560 --> 00:01:45,560
Huh?

23
00:01:58,380 --> 00:02:09,060
THE WORLD'S STRONGEST REARGUARD

24
00:03:16,960 --> 00:03:21,970
A NOVICE SEEKER IN LABYRINTH COUNTRY

25
00:03:34,690 --> 00:03:37,220
So this is the guild?

26
00:03:38,030 --> 00:03:41,710
Well, I came here like 
she told me to, so...

27
00:03:51,110 --> 00:03:52,320
That lady...

28
00:03:52,940 --> 00:03:55,710
I think she was on the bus with me.

29
00:03:56,310 --> 00:04:00,260
Ms. Suzuna Shiromiya, thank you 
for filling out the paperwork.

30
00:04:00,600 --> 00:04:04,490
I see the job you're hoping 
for is Shrine Maiden.

31
00:04:04,490 --> 00:04:06,120
Congratulations!

32
00:04:06,120 --> 00:04:09,720
I've assessed your aptitude, 
and your request was accepted.

33
00:04:14,590 --> 00:04:15,940
Hey, got a minute?

34
00:04:18,030 --> 00:04:21,450
Uh, y-yes... Can I help you?

35
00:04:21,450 --> 00:04:24,290
I'm new in this town...

36
00:04:24,290 --> 00:04:27,720
I know. Anyone who's 
registering at this guild

37
00:04:27,720 --> 00:04:30,700
is a novice who just reincarnated here.

38
00:04:31,450 --> 00:04:34,160
I'm looking for someone 
with a rearguard job.

39
00:04:34,590 --> 00:04:38,010
There's a part of my vanguard 
job that's... not the best.

40
00:04:38,010 --> 00:04:41,960
It might not be easy for a novice 
like you to team up with me...

41
00:04:41,970 --> 00:04:45,720
Check it out. Elitia's trying 
to recruit people again.

42
00:04:42,490 --> 00:04:47,300
B-But if you join a party, 
you should level up quickly.

43
00:04:45,720 --> 00:04:48,340
Wonder how many days this one'll last.

44
00:04:49,000 --> 00:04:52,850
So please form a party with me!

45
00:04:53,480 --> 00:04:54,320
Huh?

46
00:04:54,690 --> 00:04:56,340
No matter how strong she is,

47
00:04:56,340 --> 00:04:59,680
as long as she has <i>that</i>, it's 
always gonna end the same way.

48
00:05:01,420 --> 00:05:03,470
What does that mean?

49
00:05:07,640 --> 00:05:10,630
Thank you for inviting me.

50
00:05:11,210 --> 00:05:13,160
S-So you'll do it?

51
00:05:15,010 --> 00:05:16,290
Thanks!

52
00:05:16,860 --> 00:05:20,430
Okay, first of all, let's go 
get some tea or something!

53
00:05:21,370 --> 00:05:22,750
Sir...

54
00:05:23,170 --> 00:05:25,710
You have an unregistered license?

55
00:05:25,950 --> 00:05:27,760
Oh... Yes.

56
00:05:27,760 --> 00:05:29,420
Then please step right up.

57
00:05:32,700 --> 00:05:36,550
I'll take care of 
your Seeker registration

58
00:05:36,550 --> 00:05:39,840
and provide any advice you may need.

59
00:05:39,840 --> 00:05:42,020
My name is Louisa Farmel.

60
00:05:42,570 --> 00:05:46,850
Here in Labyrinth Country, only 
those who register as Seekers

61
00:05:46,850 --> 00:05:50,280
are permitted to enter labyrinths.

62
00:05:50,690 --> 00:05:53,160
For starters, please 
present your license.

63
00:05:53,800 --> 00:05:56,780
Um... before that, can you tell me...

64
00:05:57,010 --> 00:06:00,080
What is "Labyrinth Country," exactly?

65
00:06:00,340 --> 00:06:04,690
Labyrinth Country is a nation 
that is home only to Seekers,

66
00:06:04,690 --> 00:06:07,720
who explore labyrinths, and 
those who support them.

67
00:06:07,980 --> 00:06:12,710
People whose souls reincarnate 
into Labyrinth Country

68
00:06:12,710 --> 00:06:15,260
begin new lives here as Seekers.

69
00:06:15,970 --> 00:06:19,180
Reincarnate? Seeker?

70
00:06:19,670 --> 00:06:23,720
Yeah, I guess I really 
did die back there.

71
00:06:25,300 --> 00:06:27,200
S-Sir?

72
00:06:27,720 --> 00:06:31,650
Your memories are in disarray because 
you only just reincarnated.

73
00:06:31,910 --> 00:06:34,990
I'm sorry I explained things in 
such depth right off the bat.

74
00:06:34,990 --> 00:06:37,110
Would you like to be seen by a Healer?

75
00:06:37,110 --> 00:06:39,810
Oh... No, I'm all right.

76
00:06:39,810 --> 00:06:42,140
It was just a bit of a headache.

77
00:06:43,150 --> 00:06:47,580
So, um... the first thing I 
need to do is register, right?

78
00:06:48,970 --> 00:06:53,720
You'll find that the "Job" line 
on your license is blank.

79
00:06:53,980 --> 00:06:57,340
Please write the job you think 
you are most suited for,

80
00:06:57,340 --> 00:07:01,430
or the one you most want 
to try, in that blank.

81
00:07:01,430 --> 00:07:04,910
So I'm not choosing from 
a specific set of jobs?

82
00:07:05,130 --> 00:07:09,020
People reincarnate here with all 
sorts of different backgrounds.

83
00:07:09,020 --> 00:07:11,950
This system allows us to 
make the most of that.

84
00:07:12,360 --> 00:07:15,860
<i>Whether or not I'm able to get 
a job that's in high demand</i>

85
00:07:16,170 --> 00:07:19,330
<i>will determine whether I get off 
to a good start or a bad one.</i>

86
00:07:19,330 --> 00:07:23,530
Please take all the time 
you need to think it over.

87
00:07:24,000 --> 00:07:26,450
<i>A job, huh?</i>

88
00:07:27,360 --> 00:07:30,710
Atobe-kun! I have an idea 
for a really cool project!

89
00:07:30,970 --> 00:07:35,180
ATOBE-KUN!

90
00:07:31,020 --> 00:07:33,270
Give me any thoughts you may have!

91
00:07:33,270 --> 00:07:35,170
I'll use 'em all!

92
00:07:35,550 --> 00:07:38,880
<i>Before I reincarnated, I was 
worked to the bone every day</i>

93
00:07:36,180 --> 00:07:39,640
LET'S GO!!

94
00:07:37,680 --> 00:07:39,640
ATOBE-KUN

95
00:07:38,880 --> 00:07:43,110
<i>by an elite boss who was younger 
than me. Work was hell.</i>

96
00:07:43,500 --> 00:07:47,560
<i>But now I'm in Labyrinth 
Country, a different world.</i>

97
00:07:47,860 --> 00:07:50,830
<i>I won't have to work under a 
high-powered career woman,</i>

98
00:07:50,830 --> 00:07:53,530
<i>and I'm free from the 
shackles of that company.</i>

99
00:08:00,180 --> 00:08:04,260
<i>For now, I just want to set myself 
up for a nice, easy life.</i>

100
00:08:04,730 --> 00:08:06,080
Atobe-kun!

101
00:08:08,440 --> 00:08:11,710
Gah! Chief Igarashi!

102
00:08:11,710 --> 00:08:13,880
What do you mean, "gah"?

103
00:08:13,880 --> 00:08:18,220
Oh, sorry... I guess, since you're 
here, you must've also...

104
00:08:18,220 --> 00:08:23,050
Yeah. I died back home 
and reincarnated here.

105
00:08:23,410 --> 00:08:27,600
Everything I see here makes me think 
this is some cosplay world...

106
00:08:28,400 --> 00:08:31,330
but we'll be starting our 
new lives here, huh?

107
00:08:33,480 --> 00:08:38,740
Though it hasn't really hit me yet that 
I'll have to fight monsters and stuff.

108
00:08:38,740 --> 00:08:40,570
What? Monsters?!

109
00:08:41,000 --> 00:08:45,080
That's one of the things people 
who reincarnate here do for work.

110
00:08:45,080 --> 00:08:51,060
Here, your job and who you party up 
with are matters of life and death.

111
00:08:51,060 --> 00:08:53,050
Yes, I guess so.

112
00:08:53,320 --> 00:08:56,590
Atobe-kun, have you not 
picked your job yet?

113
00:08:57,060 --> 00:09:02,430
If you could get one that gives me 
someone to turn to, that'd be great.

114
00:09:02,920 --> 00:09:06,020
Um... incidentally, Chief, 
what job did you pick?

115
00:09:06,020 --> 00:09:08,660
Me? I'm...

116
00:09:09,120 --> 00:09:10,600
Actually...

117
00:09:10,600 --> 00:09:14,560
we're not boss and 
subordinate anymore, so...

118
00:09:14,870 --> 00:09:17,530
Instead of "Chief"...

119
00:09:19,000 --> 00:09:21,280
N-Nothing! Never mind!

120
00:09:21,280 --> 00:09:23,320
My job is Valkyrie.

121
00:09:23,720 --> 00:09:25,520
I can use swords and spears,

122
00:09:25,520 --> 00:09:28,290
and apparently, I'll be able 
to use some spirit magic.

123
00:09:28,510 --> 00:09:31,410
That sounds like a pretty impressive job.

124
00:09:31,410 --> 00:09:34,750
I figure I'll have a better chance at 
surviving if I can do lots of things.

125
00:09:35,090 --> 00:09:38,690
The most crucial point of a party is 
how roles within it are divided up,

126
00:09:38,690 --> 00:09:41,670
so you want to avoid having multiple 
people with the same job.

127
00:09:41,670 --> 00:09:45,260
I see. Thank you for the lesson.

128
00:09:45,260 --> 00:09:49,040
Then I should choose something that'll 
make me useful to my partymates.

129
00:09:49,040 --> 00:09:50,710
Your partymates?

130
00:09:50,710 --> 00:09:53,910
Huh? Oh, er, I mean...

131
00:09:53,910 --> 00:09:58,940
I-If we both manage to survive, 
let's meet up again somewhere,

132
00:09:59,380 --> 00:10:00,950
Chief Igarashi.

133
00:10:03,000 --> 00:10:07,250
Got it! I should hurry up and find 
some partymates myself, then!

134
00:10:13,610 --> 00:10:17,470
<i>She didn't seem like her usual self...</i>

135
00:10:18,390 --> 00:10:20,850
Hey, I'm sure she'll be fine.

136
00:10:20,850 --> 00:10:23,330
Well? Have you decided?

137
00:10:23,970 --> 00:10:26,090
Oh, um...

138
00:10:26,370 --> 00:10:31,190
In that case, I'll explain 
a bit more about jobs.

139
00:10:31,190 --> 00:10:36,020
A Seeker's job directly affects 
their Contribution Points.

140
00:10:36,020 --> 00:10:37,140
Contribution Points?

141
00:10:37,140 --> 00:10:39,660
Bringing back rare treasures,

142
00:10:39,660 --> 00:10:41,700
defeating strong monsters,

143
00:10:41,700 --> 00:10:43,930
saving a companion's life...

144
00:10:43,930 --> 00:10:48,360
Performing such actions in labyrinths 
will earn you Contribution Points.

145
00:10:48,730 --> 00:10:49,750
And...

146
00:10:50,160 --> 00:10:55,210
the number of points you have determines 
your place in the Seeker hierarchy.

147
00:10:55,210 --> 00:11:01,260
SEEKING RESULTS

148
00:10:55,860 --> 00:11:01,260
Your activities in labyrinths are 
recorded and displayed on this page.

149
00:10:56,090 --> 00:11:01,260
NO RESULTS TO DISPLAY YET

150
00:11:01,530 --> 00:11:04,720
<i>Wow, it's almost like a tablet.</i>

151
00:11:04,960 --> 00:11:08,110
The hierarchy determines your 
status in Labyrinth Country,

152
00:11:08,110 --> 00:11:12,740
the food, shelter, and clothing you 
get, and various other things.

153
00:11:12,740 --> 00:11:16,940
People at the bottom sometimes 
have to live in stables.

154
00:11:16,940 --> 00:11:19,320
I'd rather avoid that...

155
00:11:20,070 --> 00:11:21,320
Um, Louisa-san...

156
00:11:21,640 --> 00:11:25,020
Are rearguard jobs in high 
demand, even for novices?

157
00:11:25,020 --> 00:11:28,550
Yes, a rearguard is 
essential to any party,

158
00:11:28,550 --> 00:11:32,640
but they have lower stamina and defense 
than vanguard and midguard jobs,

159
00:11:32,640 --> 00:11:36,000
so they're less likely to still 
be around in five years.

160
00:11:36,320 --> 00:11:40,210
That means there's always a 
demand for rearguard jobs.

161
00:11:40,690 --> 00:11:45,950
<i>If they're in demand, it might be worth 
choosing one, despite the risks.</i>

162
00:11:46,830 --> 00:11:49,890
<i>What rearguard job would I be good in?</i>

163
00:11:50,700 --> 00:11:52,990
<i>Maybe if I just put "Rearguard,"</i>

164
00:11:52,990 --> 00:11:55,950
<i>it'll automatically pick the 
one I'm most cut out for...</i>

165
00:11:54,850 --> 00:11:57,820
REARGUARD

166
00:12:03,790 --> 00:12:04,720
Huh?

167
00:12:05,070 --> 00:12:06,120
Huh?

168
00:12:06,120 --> 00:12:08,620
Let me just take a quick look at this...

169
00:12:09,820 --> 00:12:12,500
What in the world did you write?

170
00:12:12,500 --> 00:12:14,370
"Rearguard."

171
00:12:24,840 --> 00:12:27,130
Congratulations, Mr. Atobe!

172
00:12:27,130 --> 00:12:29,630
Your request has been accepted!

173
00:12:31,620 --> 00:12:34,570
Uh, h-hang on a minute, Louisa-san!

174
00:12:36,380 --> 00:12:39,060
Just... what job did I end up getting?

175
00:12:39,330 --> 00:12:41,860
Y-You're a Rearguard.

176
00:12:41,860 --> 00:12:44,910
At least... I think you're a Rearguard.

177
00:12:44,900 --> 00:12:47,950
SWORDSMAN

178
00:12:45,320 --> 00:12:49,360
To be honest, I've never 
seen this language before.

179
00:12:49,360 --> 00:12:53,870
Normally, whatever a Seeker 
writes stays as it was written.

180
00:12:54,110 --> 00:12:57,750
But when it's a job that 
has no precedent, well...

181
00:12:57,750 --> 00:13:00,890
I know I told you it was 
always in demand, but...

182
00:13:01,270 --> 00:13:04,340
You might find it difficult 
to form a party.

183
00:13:06,930 --> 00:13:10,410
I consider myself partly responsible 
for giving you that advice,

184
00:13:10,410 --> 00:13:12,180
so I'll enact special measures.

185
00:13:12,810 --> 00:13:15,810
Until you figure out 
your job's strengths,

186
00:13:15,810 --> 00:13:18,420
please use these Mercenary Tickets.

187
00:13:22,780 --> 00:13:24,240
DEFENSE SUPPORT LV. 1: REDUCES INJURY 
TO PARTY MEMBERS IN FRONT BY 10 POINTS

188
00:13:23,960 --> 00:13:27,030
<i>So the skills I can acquire are...</i>

189
00:13:24,240 --> 00:13:25,470
ATTACK SUPPORT LV. 1: 
ADDS 10 INJURY POINTS TO ATTACKS
 BY PARTY MEMBERS IN FRONT

190
00:13:25,470 --> 00:13:26,700
SUPPORT RECOVERY LV. 1:
 RESTORES 5 VITALITY POINTS EVERY
 30 SECONDS TO PARTY MEMBERS IN FRONT

191
00:13:26,700 --> 00:13:28,240
REAR VIEW: SPENDS 5 MAGIC POINTS
 TO EXPAND YOUR VISION TO COVER YOUR
 REAR FOR A SET PERIOD OF TIME

192
00:13:28,430 --> 00:13:32,030
<i>How much is ten points of damage, anyway?</i>

193
00:13:32,460 --> 00:13:39,290
<i>I guess "Rear View" allows a rearguard 
with low stamina to watch the rear.</i>

194
00:13:39,710 --> 00:13:41,730
<i>That sounds useful, too,</i>

195
00:13:41,730 --> 00:13:45,230
<i>but the one I should take first 
is is Defense Support 1,</i>

196
00:13:45,230 --> 00:13:50,060
<i>and after testing that out, Support 
Recovery 1, so I can heal...</i>

197
00:13:50,060 --> 00:13:52,550
<i>No, I'll put that one on hold.</i>

198
00:13:52,550 --> 00:13:56,720
<i>I'll find out if there are potions 
or other ways to heal first.</i>

199
00:13:57,220 --> 00:14:01,310
<i>Okay, I'll put some points 
into Defense Support 1 first.</i>

200
00:14:04,020 --> 00:14:07,360
No noticeable changes...

201
00:14:07,720 --> 00:14:11,030
Maybe once I'm in a party 
I'll know for sure

202
00:14:11,030 --> 00:14:14,820
whether I picked wrong 
or if things will work out.

203
00:14:20,520 --> 00:14:22,080
I'm Leila.

204
00:14:22,650 --> 00:14:25,920
Assistant manager of 
the Mercenary Office.

205
00:14:26,440 --> 00:14:29,890
Um... I'd like to use these tickets.

206
00:14:30,330 --> 00:14:32,880
I can give you a demi-human for those.

207
00:14:32,880 --> 00:14:37,230
I'd prefer a vanguard. One who 
can use a shield, if possible.

208
00:14:37,230 --> 00:14:38,090
Mm.

209
00:14:38,430 --> 00:14:42,060
All we've got left is a female Lizardman.

210
00:14:42,060 --> 00:14:43,860
Lizardman?

211
00:14:43,860 --> 00:14:45,390
She's a Rogue.

212
00:14:45,390 --> 00:14:47,630
She can use most equipment 
to some degree,

213
00:14:47,630 --> 00:14:49,860
and she wears a leather buckler.

214
00:14:49,860 --> 00:14:54,940
She should be plenty useful on the 
first floor, the Field of Dawn, up ahead.

215
00:14:54,940 --> 00:14:56,330
I see.

216
00:14:56,630 --> 00:15:00,150
<i>I guess I should start by testing out</i>

217
00:15:00,150 --> 00:15:02,700
<i>Defense Support 1 on some weak monsters.</i>

218
00:15:03,400 --> 00:15:06,780
All right, I'd like to hire 
this Lizardman, please.

219
00:15:06,780 --> 00:15:07,910
Mm.

220
00:15:12,570 --> 00:15:14,630
A Lizardman, huh?

221
00:15:15,760 --> 00:15:18,130
So... something like this?

222
00:15:20,040 --> 00:15:21,430
Sorry for the wait.

223
00:15:25,570 --> 00:15:26,430
Huh?

224
00:15:27,450 --> 00:15:28,340
Huh?!

225
00:15:29,940 --> 00:15:34,950
THE WORLD'S STRONGEST REARGUARD

226
00:15:31,560 --> 00:15:34,430
Rearguard is a job I'll 
guard close to my heart.

227
00:15:34,950 --> 00:15:39,950
THE WORLD'S STRONGEST REARGUARD

228
00:15:37,570 --> 00:15:39,360
Uh... hello?

229
00:15:40,830 --> 00:15:42,470
Her name's Theresia.

230
00:15:43,700 --> 00:15:46,890
A... human girl?

231
00:15:46,890 --> 00:15:49,430
Former human, to be exact.

232
00:15:49,430 --> 00:15:50,210
Huh?

233
00:15:50,490 --> 00:15:54,300
A demi-human is what a human 
transforms into after being

234
00:15:54,300 --> 00:15:56,270
killed by a monster in a labyrinth.

235
00:15:57,130 --> 00:16:02,140
That's part of why they say the dead 
can't be revived in Labyrinth Country.

236
00:16:02,710 --> 00:16:06,980
If this transformation can be undone, 
they can return to their original form.

237
00:16:07,230 --> 00:16:11,110
But you treat her as a Lizardman now?

238
00:16:11,430 --> 00:16:16,200
Well, it's not illegal to put 
the slave crest on demi-humans.

239
00:16:16,850 --> 00:16:19,340
We can't communicate with them.

240
00:16:19,340 --> 00:16:23,170
In general, they can only act 
on the orders we give them.

241
00:16:23,820 --> 00:16:28,120
Though they do fight instinctively 
when combat breaks out.

242
00:16:29,090 --> 00:16:32,370
<i>I definitely didn't see this coming.</i>

243
00:16:33,600 --> 00:16:37,000
Well, my name is Arihito.

244
00:16:37,000 --> 00:16:38,610
Nice to meet you, Theresia.

245
00:16:47,900 --> 00:16:49,870
<i>Well, I have a weapon now.</i>

246
00:16:49,870 --> 00:16:52,940
<i>I'm finally starting to 
look like a Seeker...</i>

247
00:16:53,370 --> 00:16:57,540
<i>but I feel bad making a little 
girl like this fight.</i>

248
00:16:58,500 --> 00:17:02,180
I'll find some weak monsters 
to test my skills on,

249
00:17:02,180 --> 00:17:04,160
then call it an early day.

250
00:17:06,070 --> 00:17:09,950
So that's the first 
labyrinth, Field of Dawn.

251
00:17:14,000 --> 00:17:16,450
Oh, another novice, huh?

252
00:17:17,260 --> 00:17:21,290
He's Japanese, just like the Valkyrie 
in that last party we saw.

253
00:17:21,290 --> 00:17:23,180
Oh, yeah, that hottie.

254
00:17:23,440 --> 00:17:25,960
<i>A Japanese Valkyrie?</i>

255
00:17:25,960 --> 00:17:28,430
<i>That must be Chief Igarashi.</i>

256
00:17:28,430 --> 00:17:30,660
<i>I guess she formed a party quick.</i>

257
00:17:30,940 --> 00:17:32,740
I'm Ribault.

258
00:17:32,740 --> 00:17:35,240
I make a living finding 
people in labyrinths

259
00:17:35,240 --> 00:17:38,110
who can't move anymore and rescuing them.

260
00:17:38,390 --> 00:17:42,110
H-Hello. My name is Arihito.

261
00:17:42,500 --> 00:17:44,090
It's nice to meet you.

262
00:17:44,550 --> 00:17:46,450
Um, Ribault-san...

263
00:17:46,750 --> 00:17:50,950
Since you rescue people, does that mean 
it's dangerous inside labyrinths?

264
00:17:50,950 --> 00:17:54,040
Not really, as long as you don't 
take on enemies you can't handle.

265
00:17:54,310 --> 00:17:56,800
You have a mercenary with you,

266
00:17:56,800 --> 00:17:59,210
so if you stick to low-level monsters,

267
00:17:59,210 --> 00:18:02,680
you'll make it out on your own 
as long as you're careful.

268
00:18:04,210 --> 00:18:05,510
Just...

269
00:18:05,510 --> 00:18:07,870
watch out for Named monsters.

270
00:18:07,870 --> 00:18:09,220
Named monsters?

271
00:18:09,220 --> 00:18:13,700
Any novice who takes on one 
of those is gonna die.

272
00:18:13,960 --> 00:18:15,770
If you see one, run straight outta there.

273
00:18:15,770 --> 00:18:17,060
They die?

274
00:18:17,710 --> 00:18:22,520
Understood. Thank you for 
that important lesson.

275
00:18:22,800 --> 00:18:25,380
There are other parties in there, too,

276
00:18:25,380 --> 00:18:28,150
and if you're in a pinch, just call us.

277
00:18:28,430 --> 00:18:32,060
We patrol regularly, but we can't 
be in there around the clock.

278
00:18:32,060 --> 00:18:33,060
Got it.

279
00:18:36,040 --> 00:18:37,190
<i>Right...</i>

280
00:18:38,060 --> 00:18:39,180
Theresia.

281
00:18:40,200 --> 00:18:41,090
Let's go.

282
00:19:22,380 --> 00:19:24,740
Is that fluffball a monster?

283
00:19:27,350 --> 00:19:30,680
ENCOUNTERED MONSTER: COTTON BALL 
LV. 1 — DROPS: ??? — CAUTION

284
00:19:27,740 --> 00:19:30,690
Cotton Ball, level 1...

285
00:19:33,140 --> 00:19:36,490
Is this one of the monsters 
Ribault talked about?

286
00:19:45,200 --> 00:19:46,660
<i>You're kidding me...</i>

287
00:19:46,660 --> 00:19:49,160
<i>It hits that hard at level 1?</i>

288
00:19:49,530 --> 00:19:52,260
Let's run from this one, Theresia!

289
00:19:53,950 --> 00:19:54,950
Theresia?!

290
00:19:57,550 --> 00:20:00,340
<i>Her life itself is being whittled down!</i>

291
00:20:01,220 --> 00:20:02,040
Wai—

292
00:20:11,420 --> 00:20:15,980
<i>What am I doing, letting a little 
girl like her protect me?</i>

293
00:20:16,350 --> 00:20:21,040
<i>I have to do something... but 
what can I do as a Rearguard?</i>

294
00:20:22,610 --> 00:20:27,030
DEFENSE SUPPORT LV. 1: REDUCES INJURY 
TO PARTY MEMBERS IN FRONT BY 10 POINTS

295
00:20:23,220 --> 00:20:27,030
<i>Defense Support... That's it!</i>

296
00:20:31,830 --> 00:20:33,910
Theresia, I'll back you up!

297
00:20:35,830 --> 00:20:37,330
DEFENSE SUPPORT LV. 1

298
00:20:38,880 --> 00:20:40,540
Okay, Theresia!

299
00:20:40,830 --> 00:20:42,860
Make your move after I shoot it!

300
00:20:57,230 --> 00:20:59,610
D-Did we beat it?

301
00:21:03,250 --> 00:21:06,180
I should have used my 
skill right at the start.

302
00:21:07,140 --> 00:21:09,000
Are you okay with those wounds?

303
00:21:09,000 --> 00:21:11,350
Should we exit for now and heal up?

304
00:21:15,830 --> 00:21:17,480
I'm sorry, Theresia.

305
00:21:17,860 --> 00:21:21,160
To be honest, I wasn't 
taking this seriously.

306
00:21:21,160 --> 00:21:24,010
Dying in a fight like this 
wasn't even on my radar.

307
00:21:24,010 --> 00:21:25,970
I finally understand now.

308
00:21:26,780 --> 00:21:28,890
Thanks for protecting me.

309
00:21:29,290 --> 00:21:32,020
From now on, I'll do my 
part to protect you, too.

310
00:21:37,300 --> 00:21:38,370
What's that?!

311
00:21:43,520 --> 00:21:45,350
Chief Igarashi?

312
00:21:45,650 --> 00:21:48,640
Is her party fighting something?

313
00:21:55,110 --> 00:21:56,670
A Redface...

314
00:21:56,670 --> 00:22:00,550
Damn it! Why is a Named monster here?!

315
00:22:00,550 --> 00:22:02,150
Named?

316
00:22:04,170 --> 00:22:05,710
BOOMERANG DIVE

317
00:22:07,170 --> 00:22:08,740
Chief Igarashi!

